WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.846
In Insidious One, I pointed out ghosts that were hiding in the background of scenes,

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:06.282
and the second movie would contain an even more, well hidden, spirit.

00:00:06.346 --> 00:00:09.278
There's a scene where Renai is on the phone, and as she walks past, you can

00:00:09.284 --> 00:00:11.262
see the woman in white sitting in the living room.

00:00:11.316 --> 00:00:14.110
But once she reaches the doorframe, the apparition is gone.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:17.566
Director James Wan and screenwriter Leigh Whannell explained why they do this on

00:00:17.588 --> 00:00:19.034
Insidious Chapter Two's Blu ray.

00:00:19.082 --> 00:00:22.382
The idea is if one audience member catches it and reacts, then their friends

00:00:22.436 --> 00:00:25.394
will go, what? What did you see? And the tension in the movie theater builds.

00:00:25.442 --> 00:00:28.946
Personally, outside of theater experience, I always find it creepy

00:00:28.978 --> 00:00:31.782
to go back and discover something that's not supposed to be there.

00:00:31.836 --> 00:00:34.946
So in this video, I'll be going over all of the things you might have missed

00:00:34.978 --> 00:00:38.502
in Insidious Chapter Two. To learn about the artifacts in Elise's basement

00:00:38.566 --> 00:00:40.182
and more Insidious secrets.

00:00:40.246 --> 00:00:42.380
Stick around to the end of this video.

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:46.995
🎵Metal Music🎵

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:51.370
This baby stroller looks like Pac-Man, and I'm tired of not talking about it.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:55.094
Welcome to Things You Missed, James Wan, Leigh Whannell, and just about everyone

00:00:55.152 --> 00:00:57.482
from the first Insidious came back for the sequel.

00:00:57.546 --> 00:00:59.594
For Wan, it was his first time directing a sequel.

00:00:59.642 --> 00:01:02.734
Whannell had experience with sequels, having penned the 2nd and 3rd Saw movies

00:01:02.772 --> 00:01:05.854
and even a miniseries called Insidious Spectral Sightings about

00:01:05.892 --> 00:01:08.590
Specs and Tucker's paranormal adventures before meeting Elise.

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:10.562
If you haven't seen it, don't worry too much.

00:01:10.616 --> 00:01:13.934
It's pretty boring and was rendered non canon by the events of

00:01:13.982 --> 00:01:14.626
Insidious Chapter Three.

00:01:14.728 --> 00:01:17.570
Chapter Two, unfortunately, isn't my favorite either.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:20.198
I knew something was weird with this one when I heard the younger version of

00:01:20.204 --> 00:01:23.138
Elise dubbed over with the voice of the 70 year old Lin Shaye.

00:01:23.234 --> 00:01:27.990
-[Elise] See things, things no living person is supposed to see.

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:31.390
There's actually a UK version of the trailer that includes the original

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:33.130
lines from the younger Elise.

00:01:33.548 --> 00:01:36.121
-[Elise] He sees things. No living person is supposed to see. 

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:38.214
I wish they just stuck with that in the movie.

00:01:38.262 --> 00:01:41.114
I think the audience is smart enough to understand who Elise is and

00:01:41.152 --> 00:01:44.694
understand that people's voices can change over time, except Rivers Cuomo.

00:01:44.742 --> 00:01:47.850
Despite that, the expanded characterization for Elise is appreciated.

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:50.542
We get to see her house for the first time, which happens to be the perfect

00:01:50.596 --> 00:01:53.310
place to jump into some more Things You Missed.

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:55.059
🎵Slice🎵

00:01:55.188 --> 00:01:58.179
🎵Mysterious Music🎵

00:01:58.370 --> 00:02:01.314
In my episode on the first movie, I talked about the red door, which

00:02:01.352 --> 00:02:04.270
connected the Lambert's house in the Further to the layer of the demon.

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:07.890
We see another red door marking the main antagonist here in Chapter Two.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:10.606
So it makes sense that when we enter the home of the franchise's

00:02:10.638 --> 00:02:13.730
Ghost Whisperer, Elise, we must enter through these big red gates.

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:16.726
She used to do her psychic readings at home, so the red entryways are

00:02:16.748 --> 00:02:19.158
probably meant to be inviting to spirits on the other side.

00:02:19.244 --> 00:02:22.198
Now that we've seen a couple examples of the color red representing the

00:02:22.204 --> 00:02:25.226
gateway between the living and the dead, I'm reminded of another movie that

00:02:25.248 --> 00:02:29.034
used the color in the same way, The Sixth Sense, which had red doorknobs,

00:02:29.072 --> 00:02:32.602
red flowers, red tents, and more to show the connection between our world

00:02:32.656 --> 00:02:33.414
and the world of the dead.

00:02:33.462 --> 00:02:37.006
Elise's basement, where she does her readings, is also covered in red,

00:02:37.028 --> 00:02:38.794
Just like the demonic layer in Insidious.

00:02:38.922 --> 00:02:41.966
The basement is decked out with paraphernalia artifacts, which serve as

00:02:41.988 --> 00:02:45.086
this franchise's version of the artifact room from the Conjuring, which had

00:02:45.108 --> 00:02:46.314
come out just two months earlier.

00:02:46.362 --> 00:02:49.326
Elise may have died at the end of the first movie, but her presence is still felt,

00:02:49.348 --> 00:02:52.046
and she seems to leave a message for Specs and Tucker.

00:02:52.078 --> 00:02:55.966
They find an old tape and put it into her Panasonic VHS player, but several

00:02:55.998 --> 00:02:59.118
letters on the logo are crossed out, causing it to read Panic.

00:02:59.214 --> 00:03:02.354
After possessing Josh Lambert's body, the Bride in Black tried to convince

00:03:02.402 --> 00:03:05.122
Renai that everything was fine and that she should not panic.

00:03:05.186 --> 00:03:08.290
So this was Elise's way of saying, don't listen to him panic.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:11.106
The reading room also contains a mannequin wearing a gas mask.

00:03:11.138 --> 00:03:14.454
A callback to the gas mask seance that Elise performed in the first movie.

00:03:14.502 --> 00:03:18.074
The second film introduces a new psychic character, Carl, who has his own

00:03:18.112 --> 00:03:21.158
unique way of contacting the dead using these Ouija dice.

00:03:21.254 --> 00:03:24.902
Another common element this one shares with Insidious is the cinematography.

00:03:24.966 --> 00:03:27.822
In the previous episode, I pointed out how the camera was always moving

00:03:27.876 --> 00:03:30.606
through doorframes and looking through doorframes in the real world to

00:03:30.628 --> 00:03:33.402
highlight the bright openness of the real world, in contrast to the dark,

00:03:33.466 --> 00:03:35.050
closed off nature of the Further.

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:38.234
We see more of that in Chapter Two, as well as more evidence that the doors

00:03:38.282 --> 00:03:39.822
are used to link these two worlds.

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:43.186
For example, Carl gets a vision of the antagonist Parker Crane when he

00:03:43.208 --> 00:03:46.114
touches a doorframe at the abandoned hospital and at Parker's home,

00:03:46.152 --> 00:03:48.946
When they discover they are speaking to an evil entity, all of the doors in

00:03:48.968 --> 00:03:50.222
the house slam shut.

00:03:50.286 --> 00:03:52.482
There are a couple more connections to the first Insidious.

00:03:52.546 --> 00:03:55.382
While Specs and Tucker are watching the tape from Josh's childhood recorded

00:03:55.436 --> 00:03:59.286
in 1986, Lorraine is at home and the movie Carnival of Souls is playing on

00:03:59.308 --> 00:03:59.762
her TV.

00:03:59.762 --> 00:04:02.534
It reminds me of something that I discovered when making a video on the

00:04:02.572 --> 00:04:04.350
Red Faced Demon from the first Insidious.

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:07.414
James Wan referred to the character as something out of a crazy mystical carnival.

00:04:07.462 --> 00:04:10.826
It sounds a lot like John, a creepy character from Carnival of Souls

00:04:10.848 --> 00:04:13.478
who even has a similar hairstyle to Red Face.

00:04:13.574 --> 00:04:17.166
The next morning, when we see the mom, Renai, wake up, the scene looks just

00:04:17.188 --> 00:04:20.666
like the introductory scene in the first movie, only this time Josh cannot

00:04:20.698 --> 00:04:22.382
be seen sleeping there beside her.

00:04:22.436 --> 00:04:24.494
Our first clue that something isn't right.

00:04:24.612 --> 00:04:27.738
Those who saw my episode on the first movie may remember that Leigh Whannell

00:04:27.754 --> 00:04:29.626
wanted to avoid any false jump scares.

00:04:29.658 --> 00:04:32.782
If they were going to release the tension, he wanted it to be a real threat.

00:04:32.846 --> 00:04:34.722
That's not the case in Insidious Chapter Two.

00:04:34.776 --> 00:04:38.062
Early on, Renai trips on this baby saucer for a cheesy scare.

00:04:38.126 --> 00:04:40.414
However, there is some significance to this scene.

00:04:40.462 --> 00:04:44.006
The saucer plays the song Row, Row, Row Your Boat, the same song that the

00:04:44.028 --> 00:04:46.950
new villain, the Woman in White, can be heard singing in the living room

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.562
shortly before abducting the baby.

00:04:48.626 --> 00:04:51.766
This demonstrates how music can be perceived in both the Further and the

00:04:51.788 --> 00:04:54.566
real world, which sets up the moment when we discover that Josh had been

00:04:54.588 --> 00:04:57.526
trying to get through to Renai by playing her song on the piano when he was

00:04:57.548 --> 00:04:58.402
trapped in the Further.

00:04:58.466 --> 00:05:00.354
There are a few more instances of foreshadowing.

00:05:00.402 --> 00:05:02.990
Dalton can be seen reading Turn of the Screw before bed.

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:04.922
This is an 1898 horror novel.

00:05:04.986 --> 00:05:08.174
Maybe you're familiar with the 2020 adaptation The Turning, or the much

00:05:08.212 --> 00:05:10.730
better 1961 adaptation The Innocence.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:14.270
Dalton is only nine or ten years old, so he has no business being interested

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:14.990
in this book.

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:18.254
However, considering his ability to see things like Elise, it's possible

00:05:18.292 --> 00:05:20.962
that his clairvoyant ability caused him to choose this book.

00:05:21.016 --> 00:05:24.274
Because when Carl, Lorraine, Specs and Tucker later investigate the old

00:05:24.312 --> 00:05:27.166
crane house, the Woman in White unscrews the chandelier, which nearly

00:05:27.198 --> 00:05:29.038
crashes down on Carl and Lorraine.

00:05:29.134 --> 00:05:32.866
Then again, he also seems to read Moby Dick, so maybe he just loves reading

00:05:32.898 --> 00:05:33.794
old classics.

00:05:33.922 --> 00:05:37.286
There may also be a moment of foreshadowing when Specs and Tucker face off

00:05:37.308 --> 00:05:39.750
in their own version of Rock, Paper, Scissors.

00:05:40.570 --> 00:05:41.778
-[Tucker] This better be the goddamn ninja.

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:43.894
-[Specs] Superior sense of smell, my friend.

00:05:44.012 --> 00:05:47.306
After arriving at the old Crane house, Specs is the first one to comment on the smell

00:05:47.328 --> 00:05:51.878
-[Specs] What is that smell?

00:05:51.894 --> 00:05:52.742
Which eventually leads them to discovering the bodies of Parker Crane's victims.

00:05:52.806 --> 00:05:56.202
One more small detail about Specs and Tucker, their van's license plate says

00:05:56.256 --> 00:06:00.234
AstralP, short for Astral Projection, the ability shared by Elise, Josh,

00:06:00.282 --> 00:06:03.006
Dalton and Lorraine, which allows them to leave their physical bodies to

00:06:03.028 --> 00:06:05.034
explore the spiritual world of the Further.

00:06:05.162 --> 00:06:08.778
I saw it with haunted, and it's not a friend, it's a parasite.

00:06:08.874 --> 00:06:10.878
I've never felt such a malignant presence.

00:06:10.974 --> 00:06:13.582
I'm guessing James Wan really likes that word, malignant.

00:06:13.646 --> 00:06:16.530
He would eventually make a whole movie about it in 2021.

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:19.346
At the time, though, it wasn't exactly a James Wan Easter egg.

00:06:19.378 --> 00:06:21.942
But that's not to say that this movie isn't brimming with them.

00:06:21.996 --> 00:06:24.630
Along with even more things you missed.

00:06:28.975 --> 00:06:33.320
🎵Haunting Music🎵

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:35.974
The first, Insidious, ends with The Bride and Black strangling,

00:06:36.022 --> 00:06:38.950
Elise, so at the beginning of the second one, there's an investigation

00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:41.622
during which Renai is interrogated by Steve Harvey.

00:06:41.686 --> 00:06:45.226
Her guest badge for the police station simply says Metropolitan Police, just

00:06:45.248 --> 00:06:48.686
like the police stations in James Wan's Saw franchise, which never seemed to

00:06:48.708 --> 00:06:49.598
specify a city.

00:06:49.684 --> 00:06:53.194
However, we do later see a newspaper that clues us in on where Insidious

00:06:53.242 --> 00:06:53.870
takes place.

00:06:53.940 --> 00:06:56.814
We've always known they live in California, but more specifically, it seems

00:06:56.852 --> 00:06:58.410
to be Newark, California.

00:06:58.490 --> 00:07:01.774
After discovering the VHS tape from Josh's childhood visit from Elise,

00:07:01.822 --> 00:07:04.222
Tucker digitizes the footage to view on his laptop.

00:07:04.286 --> 00:07:07.058
If you pause right before he pulls up the footage, you can get a glimpse at

00:07:07.064 --> 00:07:10.206
his desktop background, which is a picture of the ghost hunting duo posing

00:07:10.238 --> 00:07:11.102
with James Wan.

00:07:11.166 --> 00:07:14.246
There are also a bunch of Adobe Premiere files, a Photoshop file of

00:07:14.268 --> 00:07:17.234
something from the hospital, which they haven't been to yet in the movie,

00:07:17.282 --> 00:07:18.914
and a movie file for the videotape.

00:07:18.962 --> 00:07:22.370
For the film shoot of Insidious Two, this was clearly the media laptop,

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:25.114
something the art director could plug in anytime they needed to show

00:07:25.152 --> 00:07:25.978
something on a screen.

00:07:26.064 --> 00:07:29.606
You can tell because these files were all modified in 2013, yet the movie

00:07:29.638 --> 00:07:31.114
takes place in 2010.

00:07:31.232 --> 00:07:34.826
We weren't supposed to see this stuff, which is why it's only on screen for

00:07:34.848 --> 00:07:35.946
a fraction of a second.

00:07:36.048 --> 00:07:38.698
However, you could make the argument that the reason that they have a bunch

00:07:38.714 --> 00:07:41.834
of video and photo editing software is for their miniseries Spectral Sightings,

00:07:41.882 --> 00:07:44.522
the non Canon web series I mentioned earlier.

00:07:44.586 --> 00:07:47.866
In Insidious Chapter Three, we learned that before meeting Elise, they fake

00:07:47.898 --> 00:07:49.582
their show through fancy video editing.

00:07:49.646 --> 00:07:50.274
-[Tucker] Thanks little man.

00:07:50.312 --> 00:07:51.970
-[Tucker] Did some of my best editing on that one.

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:53.342
-[Specs] Definitely some of our best editing.

00:07:53.406 --> 00:07:57.106
As for the date modified, maybe Tucker accidentally set his laptop's date

00:07:57.128 --> 00:07:58.190
and time incorrectly.

00:07:58.270 --> 00:07:59.570
I wouldn't put it past him.

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:02.738
Insidious Two features even more of the usual James Wan tropes that we've

00:08:02.754 --> 00:08:03.478
grown to expect.

00:08:03.564 --> 00:08:06.674
He loves to include mannequins in his work, and there are two in this movie,

00:08:06.722 --> 00:08:09.350
in Elisa's reading room and in Parker Crane's old house.

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:11.634
We also know that James Wan loves creepy dolls.

00:08:11.682 --> 00:08:14.726
When we first see the child version of Parker Crane in the Further his room is

00:08:14.748 --> 00:08:17.606
filled with girl dolls, which we come to learn is because his evil mother is

00:08:17.628 --> 00:08:20.518
forcing him to act like a girl against his will to get revenge on the father.

00:08:20.524 --> 00:08:23.614
When we first see the young Parker from behind, he looks a whole lot

00:08:23.652 --> 00:08:26.746
like Annabelle, who had made her debut appearance in The Conjuring earlier

00:08:26.778 --> 00:08:27.402
that summer.

00:08:27.466 --> 00:08:30.794
Since Carl has the ability to see into the past of objects that he touches,

00:08:30.842 --> 00:08:34.026
he's able to touch Parker's veil and see his transformation into The Bride

00:08:34.058 --> 00:08:36.926
in Black, where we also see the bride's weapon of choice, a saw.

00:08:37.028 --> 00:08:39.242
However, I don't know if this was an intentional reference.

00:08:39.306 --> 00:08:42.658
If it was, he might have used a hacksaw more akin to the ones that Adam and

00:08:42.664 --> 00:08:45.422
Dr. Gordon were left with in James Wan's breakout movie.

00:08:45.486 --> 00:08:48.786
There is a weapon that Wan loves to use even more than a saw, and that would

00:08:48.808 --> 00:08:50.574
be his trusty tranquilizer needle.

00:08:50.622 --> 00:08:54.402
Jigsaw uses it in saw and its many sequels, and it's also used in Malignant.

00:08:54.466 --> 00:08:56.006
In pretty much every movie it's used in,

00:08:56.028 --> 00:08:59.286
It knocks the victims unconscious almost immediately, yet seems to be

00:08:59.308 --> 00:09:01.462
completely safe for the person being tranquilized.

00:09:01.526 --> 00:09:05.370
According to this video from Life Noggin, that only works in the movies.

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:25.596
In any event, seeing as how Insidious Chapter Two is a movie, our

00:09:25.618 --> 00:09:28.344
protagonists try to use a tranquilizer to knock out the possessed

00:09:28.392 --> 00:09:30.972
Josh Lambert, but it backfires and ends up going into Tucker.

00:09:31.036 --> 00:09:34.016
Tucker is a lot bigger than Josh, which could explain why it doesn't put him

00:09:34.038 --> 00:09:35.330
to sleep for very long.

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:41.488
As you may know, James Wan and Leigh Whannell both come from Australia, as

00:09:41.494 --> 00:09:43.984
well as cast members Rose Byrne and Angus Sampson.

00:09:44.032 --> 00:09:46.996
For this reason, during the scenes in Josh's old room, you can spot an

00:09:47.018 --> 00:09:48.612
Australian flag hanging on the wall.

00:09:48.666 --> 00:09:52.116
They also rode kangaroos to set every single day of production, all four of them.

00:09:52.138 --> 00:09:55.188
The flag certainly serves as sort of a crew reference Easter egg, and

00:09:55.194 --> 00:09:57.716
you can find more in the scene where the protagonist hunt down Parker

00:09:57.748 --> 00:09:59.732
Crane's medical file in the abandoned hospital.

00:09:59.796 --> 00:10:01.272
His physician is listed as T. Spence,

00:10:01.326 --> 00:10:04.788
which stands for Thomas Spence, Insidious Two's prop master.

00:10:04.884 --> 00:10:07.884
One of the articles, hidden away in a chest in Parker's old house, is also

00:10:07.922 --> 00:10:09.368
written by Thomas Spence.

00:10:09.464 --> 00:10:12.988
Parker's dentist is listed as Jay Garner, which stands for Jason Garner, the

00:10:12.994 --> 00:10:13.864
movie's art director.

00:10:13.912 --> 00:10:16.632
And there's another article written by Hilary Parker, an Art department

00:10:16.696 --> 00:10:17.688
production assistant.

00:10:17.784 --> 00:10:20.600
As I mentioned, I'm a much bigger fan of the first Insidious than the second.

00:10:20.610 --> 00:10:23.936
Some people fault the first movie for being too derivative, but even

00:10:23.958 --> 00:10:27.408
if it is kind of a reskin of Poltergeist, it's at least a good reskin of Poltergeist.

00:10:27.414 --> 00:10:30.860
It's scary, it's weird, and it has lovable characters.

00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:33.856
Insidious would truly continue to follow in the footsteps of the Poltergeist

00:10:33.888 --> 00:10:36.996
franchise because Chapter Two takes after Poltergeist Two.

00:10:37.098 --> 00:10:39.936
Both families temporarily move in with the grandmother, but the haunts

00:10:39.968 --> 00:10:41.860
follow them and continue to terrorize them.

00:10:41.930 --> 00:10:45.288
Both introduce a new ghostly antagonist who motivates the ghost to try to

00:10:45.294 --> 00:10:46.056
harm the family.

00:10:46.158 --> 00:10:49.336
There's even a scene where Steven, the dad in Poltergeist, swallows this

00:10:49.358 --> 00:10:52.520
supernatural parasite thing, which causes him to become possessed and attack

00:10:52.590 --> 00:10:53.140
his wife.

00:10:53.220 --> 00:10:56.036
It's very similar to the end of Insidious Chapter Two, where they confirm

00:10:56.068 --> 00:10:58.392
that Josh is possessed and he tries to kill Renai.

00:10:58.456 --> 00:11:01.612
However, the possession scene is a pretty short section of Poltergeist Two.

00:11:01.666 --> 00:11:05.224
The finale of Insidious Two takes most of its inspiration from another movie

00:11:05.272 --> 00:11:06.712
that is much more well known.

00:11:06.776 --> 00:11:09.916
It feels like a really bad redux of The Shining, and if you watch my

00:11:09.938 --> 00:11:13.376
channel, you know that I'm a huge fan of The Shining, so I won't stand for that.

00:11:13.398 --> 00:11:16.496
Once it comes out that the other characters know that Parker Crane has

00:11:16.518 --> 00:11:19.360
possessed Josh's body, he goes crazy and tries to kill them.

00:11:19.430 --> 00:11:21.964
It feels very much like he's trying to act like Jack Torrance.

00:11:22.012 --> 00:11:24.996
He's wearing this plaid bathrobe that makes me think of the plaid shirt that

00:11:25.018 --> 00:11:26.576
Jack wore during his rampage.

00:11:26.688 --> 00:11:29.776
He may be trying to act like the real Josh, whose spirit is also wearing

00:11:29.808 --> 00:11:32.612
plaid in the Further, but it just makes me think of Jack Torrance.

00:11:32.676 --> 00:11:36.360
He snoops on Carl the same way that Jack Torrence snoops on his wife.

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:45.888
-[Jack] What you got there? How do you like it? 

00:11:45.924 --> 00:11:47.704
His fake smile is clearly inspired by Jack Nicholson's faux friendliness.

00:11:47.752 --> 00:11:51.372
After losing his mind, even the way he mockingly enunciates his words seems

00:11:51.426 --> 00:11:53.740
copy pasted from Nicholson's performance.

00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:58.352
-[Josh] What have you got behind your back? Why don't you ask your dice what I have behind my back?

00:11:58.406 --> 00:12:02.320
-[Wendy] Maybe he should be taken to a doctor.

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:07.360
-[Jack] You think maybe he should be taken to a doctor?

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:16.740
He has a hand injury. He becomes woozy after getting hit with a baseball bat.

00:12:16.810 --> 00:12:19.300
He tries to bash a door down to reach and harm his family.

00:12:19.370 --> 00:12:22.568
In Insidious, it's with a fire extinguisher, and in The Shining, it's with a

00:12:22.574 --> 00:12:23.800
fire axe.

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:26.040
-[Jack] Here's Johnny.

00:12:26.380 --> 00:12:29.192
At least he didn't say, here's Joshy or something, I guess. 

00:12:29.326 --> 00:12:33.080
I like Patrick Wilson, but it's his subtlety that makes him good.

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:36.456
Asking him to replicate one of the great madman performances of all time is

00:12:36.478 --> 00:12:38.936
like asking the other Patrick Wilson to play lead guitar in Weezer.

00:12:38.968 --> 00:12:41.996
That's a bad example, because Pat is actually pretty good on

00:12:42.018 --> 00:12:43.244
guitar. They both are.

00:12:43.282 --> 00:12:44.792
And they can both play the drums.

00:12:44.856 --> 00:12:48.476
But my point is, the actor Patrick Wilson is suited to play Josh Lambert and

00:12:48.498 --> 00:12:50.160
Ed Warren, not this.

00:12:50.310 --> 00:12:51.088
-[Josh] Shut up.

00:12:51.174 --> 00:12:51.696
-[Josh] Shut up.

00:12:51.718 --> 00:12:52.928
-[Josh] Get out of my head.

00:12:53.094 --> 00:12:53.936
-[Josh] Shut up.

00:12:54.038 --> 00:12:54.880
-[Josh] Get out of here.

00:12:54.950 --> 00:12:56.272
-[Josh] Get out of my head.

00:12:56.406 --> 00:12:59.216
Sorry, I didn't mean to turn this into a movie review, but I've just been

00:12:59.238 --> 00:13:00.480
wanting to say that for a while.

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:03.232
Much like how I would like to forget Insidious Chapter Two.

00:13:03.286 --> 00:13:06.304
Carl helps hypnotize Josh and Dalton so they can forget about their

00:13:06.342 --> 00:13:09.964
abilities to astral project, which, if you ask me, is completely idiotic.

00:13:10.012 --> 00:13:12.776
Did they not learn their damn lesson the first time? What's going to happen

00:13:12.798 --> 00:13:15.828
when Dalton has a kid and he has the ability to astral project? 

00:13:15.844 --> 00:13:18.680
You're better off remembering the past so that you can try not to repeat it.

00:13:18.750 --> 00:13:21.928
The final, final scene shows Specs and Tucker on their next job and the

00:13:21.934 --> 00:13:23.892
ghost version of Elise joining them from the Further.

00:13:23.956 --> 00:13:27.304
She hears the crackling sound made by the Red Face Demon in a new house and

00:13:27.342 --> 00:13:28.932
looks up and sees something shocking.

00:13:28.996 --> 00:13:32.276
The movie ends on a cliffhanger, which I'm fine with, but then Blumhouse

00:13:32.308 --> 00:13:35.648
pulls the same BS they did with The Purge Election Year and

00:13:35.774 --> 00:13:37.324
makes two prequels before addressing that cliffhanger.

00:13:37.372 --> 00:13:40.848
However, in the case of Insidious, one of those prequels is the best film in

00:13:40.854 --> 00:13:42.864
the entire franchise, and I'm covering it next on Things You Missed.

00:13:42.902 --> 00:13:45.712
Check out that video on the left.

00:13:45.766 --> 00:13:48.880
And remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new horrors every week.

00:13:48.950 --> 00:13:52.576
Ring the death bell and select all notifications, and I will see you in the

00:13:52.598 --> 00:13:55.520
next one, assuming we both survive.

